{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgEVs3rYPWbMjeti1USt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written candidate 5 and it passes the self-check (`OK`). Convergence and speed are still unverified: the one-chain smoke fit can't give R-hat, and the production fit's 30-minute limit wasn't tested. Novelty against the live models isn't checked here either.\n\n**Which model and what changed:** I refined `iter0_candidate4`, the narrowest loser (tied with the incumbent at 1.8× dse). The one change is a person-specific decisiveness that scales every cue together: tally span, switching, the repeating-unit penalty and three-flip chunk variety. It replaces that model's person-specific sensitivity on the tally span alone. Its population mean is fixed at 1 on the log scale so the shared cue weights stay identified, and it has 400 slots so the design can still predict new participants. The idea is that some people act on their impression of randomness consistently on every pair while others choose close to a coin flip. That targets the critique's one discrepancy that survives the false-discovery correction: people differ in how often they agree with the majority choice more than the incumbent allows (q = 0.048).\n\n**Model name:** `person_decisiveness_tally_switch_triplet`\n\n**Check results:**\n- **Fit quality:** the smoke-fit ELPD-LOO was −3343.2. I ran the same check on the unmodified `iter0_candidate4`, which scored −3418.0, so this looks promising. A 100-draw single-chain fit is only a rough indicator, though.\n- **LOO reliability:** on the smoke fit, 12% of trials had Pareto k > 0.5, above the 1% tolerance, so that ELPD may be inaccurate. A short single chain often does this, but if the full fit is also flagged, the model can't be exported as the winner.\n- **Speed:** my check took about 9 minutes against 6.4 for `iter0_candidate4`, about 1.4× slower. That model passed admission's time limit, so this one should too, but that's an estimate.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_5/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74597,"cache_read_input_tokens":11602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":74597,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad176203-ff37-48dc-b3ae-8fafda46d51c","uuid":"ea98328c-4477-4afb-b328-d8d0d23de091","timestamp":"2026-10-04T00:15:47.507Z","request_id":"req_011CfgEVrfYfhQPKovUfCQvg"}
